Critical bug: `_get_asset_check_partition_status()` is an async method but is being called without `await` inside a set comprehension. This will compare a coroutine object to `status`, which will always be `False`, causing `matching_partitions` to always be empty.

The set comprehension needs to be rewritten to properly await async calls:

```python
matching_partitions = set()
for partition in from_subset.expensively_compute_partition_keys():
    partition_status = await self._get_asset_check_partition_status(key, partition)
    if partition_status == status:
        matching_partitions.add(partition)
return from_subset.compute_intersection_with_partition_keys(matching_partitions)
```
```suggestion
        matching_partitions = set()
        for partition in from_subset.expensively_compute_partition_keys():
            partition_status = await self._get_asset_check_partition_status(key, partition)
            if partition_status == status:
                matching_partitions.add(partition)
        return from_subset.compute_intersection_with_partition_keys(matching_partitions)
```


